  "notes": [
    "`tempK` kept as written: its name says kelvin, but its values run from -5.066 to -5, outside the 233.15 to 333.15 K (−40 to 60 °C) an electronics bay can have, and below 0 no temperature in kelvin can be; nothing in the file says which unit it is in",
    "`imuTemp` kept as written: its name states no unit, and every value is exactly 0, no temperature in kelvin, and a placeholder rather than a reading in any unit",
    "`accelX`, `accelY` and `accelZ` read in standard gravities, × 9.806 65 m/s², from the pad's gravity: the three axes' magnitude reads within 10% of 9.806 65 for 0.2 s of the file's time. It reads within 10% of 1 for 6.1 s. A board at rest or under a parachute reads 1 g. The unit whose 1 g lasts at least 1 s and twice as long as the other's is taken",
    "`gyroX`, `gyroY` and `gyroZ` read in degrees per second, from the board's turning: over 3 stretches of 10 steps at most 0.05 s apart with the accelerometer within 15% of 1 g, its direction turns 0.600 rad. A board at rest or under a parachute reads so. Over the same stretches, the gyroscope's rates turn the board across that direction 34.380 rad read in radians per second, 0.600 rad read in degrees. The unit whose turn is within a quarter to 4 times the accelerometer's is taken",
    "`unfiltAlt` read in meters, from the pressure: from the first sample to the one of lowest pressure it climbs 120.0. The standard atmosphere climbs 120.1 m, and the two are within 25%"
  ]
}
